<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Farrell</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Fearghail</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Farrells were an Irish ruling family who held the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annaly">Annaly</a>, in what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-longford">County Longford</a>, from the 12th century. Descended from the Uí Fergail of Tethba, they divided into rival branches but kept much of their independence until the Tudor reorganisation of the 16th century, when their lands were shired as County Longford.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ofarrell.jpg" alt="O'Farrell" width="320" height="357" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iván M. R. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27FARRELL_Coat_of_Arms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
